```

_Formula: Pain-point lead. Opens with the exact question the avatar asks himself at 3am. Highest emotional pull but loses the proof number in the first line. Use this if testing a more conversational tone._

### About

**About section**

```text
You're winning more work than ever and taking less home. The jobs are busy, the lads are flat out, and by the time the final account closes there's nowt left. You can feel it but you can't quite put your finger on where it went.

That's the problem I fix.

I spent fifteen years running operations in building services, finishing as Operations Director at Harlow & Pike where I grew the HVAC division from £4.2m to £11.8m over five years. I did that by shifting the model from one-off installs to planned maintenance contracts and tightening job pricing so margin held through growth. I didn't read about these problems. I lived them.

I now work with MDs in M&E, HVAC and electrical contracting who are stuck in the same three places:

- Margin bleeding out of jobs with no early warning and no clear cause
- MD still fielding site calls at seven in the morning because the team won't make a call without them
- Retentions sitting unpaid for months because nobody's accountable for chasing them

I work with eight contractors at a time. That's it. Because these businesses need proper time, not a slot on a conveyor belt.

From week one I get into the job reviews and pricing discussions. You won't spend the first three months explaining what a variation is or how a main contractor behaves. I already know.

The work builds a weekly numbers rhythm so you can see which jobs are making money and which are bleeding it before it's too late to do anything. It shifts decisions down to the right people so you stop being the escalation point for everything. And it gets unpaid retentions moving, because that money is already earned and it's just sitting there.

This is right for you if:

- You run an M&E, HVAC or electrical contracting business turning over £2m to £12m
- You've got 15 to 40 staff and a full order book that somehow isn't converting to more in your pocket
- You're the MD and you're still the one answering every site problem personally
- You want proper visibility on the numbers, not another report from an accountant you can't quite trust

Start with the BOSS Scorecard. It takes three minutes and shows exactly which part of the business is capping your profit right now. Link below.

Or if you'd rather just have a straight conversation, drop me a message. Prospect calls on Mondays and Thursdays from 1pm.
```

_1,847 characters. Hook lands in the first two lines before 'see more'. Written in Zander's voice: plain, direct, West Yorkshire grounded. BOSS Scorecard call to action at the close._

