### If they say not now

Do not push. Say something like: 'No problem at all. You've got a clearer picture of where things stand, and that is worth having.' Then ask if it would be useful to check back in a couple of weeks, and send a short written summary of the three or four things that came up in the session with a note on what each one is costing the business per month if it stays unresolved. Keep it specific and in their language. One of the triggers that makes MDs act is seeing the cost of standing still written down plainly. A quiet follow-up two weeks later, referencing something they said in the call, is often all it takes.
